        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays aren't just struggling; they're imploding, and the rot is now historic. <strong>A 1-10 collapse against the Giants</strong> last night capped a grotesque three-game skid where the team scored zero runs in 24 consecutive innings, tying them with the Red Sox in the loss column with 48 defeats. At 42-49 and sitting 11.5 games behind in the AL East, the Jays are running out of time to turn things around ahead of the July deadline, a reality that now feels less like pressure and more like inevitability. Pitching has been a disaster, with the bullpen imploding repeatedly, while the offense has managed just six hits across that scoreless span - no player has emerged as a solution, and the story is pure frustration. <strong>Tonight's 9:45 PM ET showdown at San Francisco</strong> offers the first real chance to reset before the pressure becomes unbearable.",
        "updated": "Updated July 7, 2026"
